PASS 1 breaker opens after N consecutive failures, a success resets the count
PASS 2 open rejects until open_for, then exactly one probe
PASS 3 a failed probe reopens; a lost probe is replaced after open_for
PASS 4 stale results are ignored (slow call cannot close an open breaker)
PASS 5 retry budget: granted retries never exceed initial + ratio*requests
PASS 6 full-jitter backoff stays in [0, min(cap, base*2^k)], mean about half
PASS 7 no outage: every policy succeeds on all requests, one remote try each
PASS 8 simulation is deterministic for a fixed seed
PASS 9 refused: edge policy beats single try; breaker cuts remote load vs P1
PASS 10 edge never serves beyond its context window, never exceeds its queue
PASS 11 edge cannot rescue prompts longer than its context
PASS 12 resume lowers mean latency vs restarting after a mid-stream drop
PASS 13 fleet, no dip: goodput about equals arrival rate for every policy
PASS 14 fleet conservation: served <= capacity, ok <= arrivals
PASS 15 fleet: shedding recovers sooner than the naive-server retry storm
PASS 16 retry budget bounds fleet retries to initial + 10% of arrivals
PASS 17 edge arithmetic hand checks
17 tests passed

